# Base harness rules

Project details: `AGENTS.md`. Harness files (this rule, skills, agents, `AGENTS.md`): **English**.
Replies to the user and all website copy: **Russian**.

## Orchestration

Non-trivial product work goes through **`/orchestrate`**. Parent chat coordinates only; it does not write requirements, implement the UI, or drive Playwright.

Pipeline (sequential, not parallel):

```
analyst → developer → tester
```

Do not add or edit MCP config (`mcp.json`). Playwright MCP is already connected.

## Subagents

| Agent | Role | Artifact |
|---|---|---|
| `analyst` | FR, then NFR, then user stories. | Always **one** file: `docs/requirements.md` (update in place, never number it). |
| `developer` | Angular frontend from those requirements. | App code + **new** `docs/impl-report-NN.md` each run (`01`, `02`, …). Never overwrite an older report. |
| `tester` | Start `npm start` → `http://localhost:4200/`, Playwright MCP vs analyst US. | **New** `docs/test-report-NN.md` each run. Read latest `impl-report-*.md`. Never overwrite an older report. |

`NN` = next integer after the highest existing file of that prefix, two digits. Developer and tester number independently.

## Handoff (subagents — STRICT)

Subagent **final message = path links only**. No summaries, excerpts, AC text, code, or explanations. The user reads files in the IDE.

Valid:

```
docs/requirements.md
docs/impl-report-02.md
```

Invalid: any prose, bullets of what was done, pasted markdown.

If a subagent replies with text → orchestrator rejects and re-delegates. Orchestrator forwards **links only** to the user (no quoting files).

One rework loop if tester fails. Then stop and report remaining gaps as links in Russian.

